        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "One of my favorite professors in college. A lot of group projects but overall pretty easy to do. ",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Phil was okay. I just felt like his 434 was not structured particularly well. He didn't spend a ton of time in class on exam topics; rather, we were expected to read a ton out of class on an online platform called ExEC",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 3
            },
            {
                "comment": "Very chill. Took his late afternoon course would let us out early everyday. 1 midterm and 1 final. Lets you have a cheat sheet for midterms. There is a group project (strategic project) (20pg paper). But not a very demanding class/pretty laid back",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "This dude is a champion. Clear, concise, and very relatable in the way he explains things. Never keeps us for the full power lecture, usually lets us out after 45 minutes. Makes the content interesting and he's very accommodating. Tests allow note sheets. Occasionally cancels class at the most clutch time. Bro of a professor.  ",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "One of my favorite business school professors. Class was easy, but I learned a lot. He drives home important points, and is available for help outside of class.",
                "difficulty_rating": 1,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
